{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "bi8Au",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Admin / Brief / Happy path band",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "fill": "$surface-container",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 22,
      "padding": 36,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "a3lK0",
          "name": "Flow title",
          "fill": "$on-surface",
          "content": "Admin — the operator's dashboard",
          "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
          "fontSize": 24,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "tYURy",
          "name": "Kit pin",
          "fill": "$outline",
          "content": "kit-version-source 0.1.1 · band 1 of 1 · happy path · 2 of 5 screens drawn",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "XiA6X",
          "name": "Purpose",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "m1I82",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Purpose",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Z30eK",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Five pages behind one sidebar, read left to right in nav order. Overview answers, in this order: what is failing, how much headroom is left, what is running now, how slow it is, what it cost, and what the traffic looked like. Request Logs is the page the operator lives in — every error row on Overview is a link into it, pre-filtered.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "ySQXf",
          "name": "Entry points",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "PcPRv",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Entry points",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "lt8bE",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "/admin/dashboard/ — Overview is the default page. Sidebar items 1 and 2 of 5 in src/admin/public/js/app.js:209. Overview → Logs is a real transition: openErrorLogs() puts a filter in the nav store and sets location.hash, so Logs opens already narrowed to that status, error code and client.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "s7ZA9",
          "name": "Screens in this band",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "CQ2Jw",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Screens in this band",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "vbl2W",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Overview / Default and Request Logs / Default, both mirrored at 6cfefe0. Request Logs is drawn with its third row expanded, because the detail panel is a state of the row rather than a screen of its own and it is where request_id, upstream status and the cache counters live. Chart INTERIORS are not mirrored on Overview: Chart.js draws a scatter and a line, the .pen layout cannot position individual points, and an approximation would look plausible while misrepresenting the shipped chart. The Logs sparkline IS drawn — it is fifteen divs with computed heights, which the layout can express honestly.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "gskz5",
          "name": "Business rules",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "UrSK7",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Business rules",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "maNao",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "One window, always: every request the pruner has not deleted, bounded at 30 days by pruneOldLogs. There is no period selector — removed 2026-09-20 because the table is already bounded and three options gave every figure its own denominator. Both Overview charts share one time axis from the oldest surviving request to just past now, marked with a dashed now line; quiet hours are drawn as zero, not skipped. Logs paginates server-side (25/50/100) and its two panels read the same single window as Overview, which is why they no longer say '60m' or 'today'. Auto-refresh every 30s on Overview; Logs re-reads only when asked.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "otdq2",
          "name": "Copy source",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "MqB2L",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Copy source",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "F7BCS8",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "src/admin/views/pages/overview.html verbatim. Numbers shown are illustrative; every label, verdict sentence and empty-state string is the code's. Timestamps render in SHELLM_TZ, default America/Mexico_City.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "P2Kx9l",
          "name": "States not drawn",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ia1G8",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "States not drawn",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "anChz",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Loading and unreachable are one-line string swaps on an otherwise empty page — 'Loading stats...' / 'Could not read stats — …' on Overview, 'Loading...' / 'Could not read the logs — …' / 'No logs found' in one table cell on Logs. They carry no layout these screens lack. The no-database answer renders Overview's window line as 'no requests recorded yet' and hides Capacity, Latency and Usage entirely. USAGE LIMIT HIT is a conditional banner above Capacity with its own colours; it is NOT drawn, because putting it on the happy path would say it is always present — it belongs to an error band this flow does not have yet. The Errors card IS drawn even though the code hides it on a clean period: triage is the reason the page is opened, and its absence is the easier state to imagine.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "E1ghK",
          "name": "Open findings",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "dGbav",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Open findings",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "NgWjW",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "D15 · D16 · D18 · D19. D19 bites hardest here: the sidebar, the active nav item and the Clear All button all use colours the kit has no name for, vendored flow-local with an UNTOKENISED suffix so the next re-vendor surfaces them instead of hiding them.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "rcUef",
          "name": "History",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
