    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "s6IUse",
      "x": -749,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Log",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "fill": "$surface-container-low",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 12,
      "padding": 28,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "j9t2ZO",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$primary-container",
          "content": "LOG",
          "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "d2lYIx",
          "name": "2026-09-20",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Flow created from the blank starter. Vendored kit 0.1.1 (37 variables: the kit's 34, kit-version-source, plus shell-surface-UNTOKENISED and nav-active-UNTOKENISED held flow-local because the kit has no name for them — see D19). Mirrored Admin / Overview / Default against src/admin/views/pages/overview.html at 6cfefe0, after the period selector was removed and both charts moved onto one time axis. Two token values were found invalid while vendoring: status-ok-fill and overlay-scrim were stored as rgba(), which the .pen schema does not accept. Fixed in both files; the kit bumped to 0.1.1.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "I38f1",
          "name": "2026-09-20b",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Added Admin / Request Logs / Default with its third row expanded. Sidebar copied from Overview and re-pointed rather than rebuilt. Two overflows found and fixed by reading bounds, not by looking: the filter row's fixed select widths left the action group no room, and a sparkline bar was taller than the box that clips it. One more untokenised colour surfaced — #3b1a1a, the Clear All background — now flow-local under D19. Mirrored after the Logs panels stopped claiming 'Last 60m' and 'Today' for a figure that covers the whole retained window.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "iuYJg",
          "name": "2026-09-20c",
          "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-20 · Sidebar rebuilt after Adrian caught two defects in it. It had an invented text wordmark where the code loads logo-dark.svg; that file is pure SVG text, so it is now mirrored exactly — '>_ ' in mono, 'She' and 'M' in white, 'LL' in primary-container. Nav labels were sentence case at 13px and are uppercase at 11px with 1.65 tracking, matching font-headline uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-[0.6875rem]. Every item now carries the 4px left border the code gives all of them (transparent when inactive), so labels no longer shift between states. The bottom row (UP uptime + docs, sign-out and GitHub links) and the page footer were missing entirely; 'last read' had been put in the sidebar, where it does not live — it belongs to the degraded banner in main, which is conditional and not drawn. Second defect: Request Logs showed two active nav items, because Update({fill: undefined}) does not clear a fill, it ignores the key. Both sidebars are now built by one function that sets every item explicitly, active or not, and a read-back asserts exactly one is active per screen.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VWK6z",
          "name": "Findings note",
          "fill": "$outline",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "D19 grew by two while mirroring the sidebar: #3b1a1a (Clear All background) and #ffffff (the logo, and text-white throughout the markup). Pure white is not on the palette — on-surface is #e0e3e7.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    }
